  <section class="section container">
    <h2>8. Data freshness and update basis</h2>
    <p>
      This page is marked <span class="badge badge--amber">September 2026 updated</span>.
      Standard VAT rates were re-checked against each member-state authority —
      Germany 19%, France 20%, the Netherlands 21%, Spain 21%, Italy 22%, Poland
      23%, Belgium 21%, Austria 20%, Sweden 25%, Portugal 23% — and the UK 20%
      rate and UKGT independence were re-checked against GOV.UK and HMRC. The
      EU-wide TARIC uniformity was re-checked against the European Commission.
      Gateway throughput and draft are 2023 port-authority snapshots; transit
      times and cost ranges are the route layer’s indicative LOW-to-MEDIUM
      estimates, not live quotes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Per-HS duty rates and unpublished fee lines stay
      <span class="muted">notPublished</span> rather than invented. The page
      therefore treats the 8% and 12% duty figures as stated worked examples,
      keeps every unpublished figure LOW, and derives every landed-cost result
      from the multiplicative formula so a reader can recompute it line by line.
    </p>
  </section>

